  "term": "distraction",
  "definition": "Distraction is a state in which attention is pulled at the same time by several disconnected objects, preventing it from being effectively focused on any one of them. In pathological use, it may also denote forms of disturbed attention arising from absent-minded preoccupation, inability to sustain concentration, or poorly organized or conflicting excitations.",
